      "writtenOn": "2020-10-20T20:40:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: why is it that DP is the only clause that cares whether the ENTRY_DONE flag is set?",
      "revId": "20fd825fe1c49759d6586b094767114364036d81",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "65533826_38d4f7fd",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 236,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-10-21T20:14:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The other modes have more complicated logic for deciding whether they\u0027re done, and it was moved inside their implementation modules. DP could probably stand to be the same way. I\u0027ll add it to the TODO list.",
      "parentUuid": "1fa7fa42_52c8f10f",
      "revId": "20fd825fe1c49759d6586b094767114364036d81",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bce82f0d_0b8eb47a",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 255,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-10-20T20:40:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we also end up here if the AP requested an invalid mode (ex. DP with a partner that doesn\u0027t report having the DP SID)?  And if so, should there be a TODO to notify of the failure?",
      "revId": "20fd825fe1c49759d6586b094767114364036d81",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ec69f178_7e610e40",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 255,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-10-21T20:14:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the AP requested an invalid mode, pd_request_enter_mode will return EC_RES_INVALID_PARAM, and the request will never be queued up.",
      "parentUuid": "bce82f0d_0b8eb47a",
      "revId": "20fd825fe1c49759d6586b094767114364036d81",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ca889fb4_b1af2922",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 255,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-10-21T20:56:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Will pd_request_enter_mode be expanding to check partner SVIDs then?  And does that open up a synchronization issue akin to the DFP check that\u0027s being done later?",
      "parentUuid": "ec69f178_7e610e40",
      "revId": "20fd825fe1c49759d6586b094767114364036d81",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "538791ed_88b0b5c0",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 255,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-10-21T21:49:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I only intend for pd_request_enter_mode to fail early in ways that were guaranteed never to succeed or that allow the subsequent code to avoid checking them again, e.g. invalid mode enums. In particular, current roles or partner state could theoretically change between queuing the request and executing it. I think it\u0027s best not to check that stuff until we\u0027re actually executing the request. And in general, if we already have a check for something that would trigger a failed mode entry, I don\u0027t think we need to check for that thing early in the command.",
      "parentUuid": "ca889fb4_b1af2922",
      "revId": "20fd825fe1c49759d6586b094767114364036d81",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
